; selftest-gate.eval - handed to the runner by `Eval.ps1 -SelfTest`; must FAIL
; with unrefused=1 and nothing else.
;
; A probe refused only by the console's GATE (no world on the title screen) has
; not met the rule it was written for, so `expect-refuse` must not count it as
; refused. It runs FIRST in its batch, before anything starts a game, and then
; ends in play so the end-state rule cannot be what fails it.
logecho on
expect-refuse worldprops start 0 0
reset
state
